    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah founded the autonomous state of Hyderabad in 1724 after defeating Mubariz Khan in the Battle of Shakarkheda.",
        "Murshid Quli Khan transferred the capital of Bengal from Dacca to Murshidabad and established a hereditary rule over the province.",
        "Farrukhsiyar issued the Golden Farman of 1717, granting extensive duty-free trading privileges to the English East India Company in Bengal.",
        "Nadir Shah of Persia invaded Delhi in 1739 during the reign of Muhammad Shah Rangeela, taking away the legendary Peacock Throne and the Koh-i-Noor diamond.",
        "The defeat of the Marathas at the Third Battle of Panipat in 1761 severely shattered their dream of replacing the Mughals as an all-India empire."
      ],
