      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Farrukhsiyar's Farman of 1717 is frequently referred to in competitive exams as the 'Magna Carta' of the East India Company in Bengal.",
        "Shah Alam II was the first Mughal emperor to become a pensioner of the British East India Company after signing the Treaty of Allahabad in 1765.",
        "Note the distinction between Successor States (Hyderabad, Bengal, Awadh) and Rebellious/New States (Marathas, Sikhs, Jats) formed during the 18th century."
